                <head>81. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On April 15, 1961, the U.N. General Assembly, by a vote of 45 to 3 with 49
                    abstentions (including the United States), adopted Resolution 1601 (XV)
                    establishing a Commission of Investigation to investigate the circumstances of
                    the death of Lumumba and his colleagues. See <hi rendition="#italic">American
                        Foreign Policy: Current Documents, 1961,</hi> page 809, for text of the
                    resolution.</p>
            </div>
